+<h2>84. issuerCerts.ts holds the admin-role test once, in one helper, <code>hasAdminRole</code> (KS-1536, groundwork)</h2>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>What this changes.</strong></td><td> KS-1536 hangs this change only because the builder needs an open ticket: it is <strong>a behaviour-preserving extraction, groundwork for the role-vocabulary class, not a fix for KS-1536</strong>. In <code>services/auth/src/routes/issuerCerts.ts</code> the four gates (<code>isAuthorisedForCertWrite</code>, <code>isAuthorisedForCertRead</code>, <code>isAuthorisedForCertRevoke</code> and <code>isAuthorisedForCertSign</code>) each copied the same two lines, <code>const role = String(user.role ?? '')</code> and the <code>ADMIN_ROLES.includes(role) || ADMIN_ROLES.includes(role.toUpperCase())</code> test. They now call one exported helper, <code>hasAdminRole(role: unknown)</code>, defined after <code>ADMIN_ROLES</code>, whose body is the same two expressions. Every spelling admitted or refused before is admitted or refused now. A local model (the Spark, DeepSeek V4 Flash, pass <code>ks_1536_p1</code>) wrote the patch; its checker passed 7 of 7 and the patch is byte-identical to the drafter&rsquo;s golden. It was applied here strictly and unchanged. </td></tr><tr><td>The product file changes +13 / &minus;8. The new test is <code>services/auth/src/__tests__/ks1536-issuer-certs-admin-role-gate-is-one-helper.test.ts</code> (vitest, 9 cells): R1 to R3 are RED at the pin (the helper is exported; it keeps the truth table of the copied lines; the file holds the role comparison once, which is a source-text check of the file), and C1 to C6 are controls on the four gates that are green before and after. No tier timing or budget in these documents moves.
+    </td></tr></table>
+<h3>84.1 Red-first, and the figures</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="4"><strong>Measured at base <code>bd6697e079fc</code>, 2026-10-28 (UTC), Kamil&rsquo;s MacBook Pro (Mac14,5, Apple M2 Max, 32 GB), shared with other sessions.</strong></td><td> vitest 4.1.12, TypeScript 5.9.3, npm 11.19.0, eslint 10.7.0, each read from the installed package. Host Node <strong>v26.8.1</strong>, which is <strong>not</strong> an LTS line, and no Node 24 run was made, so every figure below is a Node 26 measurement. </td></tr>
+<tr><td>The new file against the unfixed <code>issuerCerts.ts</code>: <strong>3 failed / 6 passed</strong> of 9, every red an <code>AssertionError</code> (R1 to R3); the six controls C1 to C6 pass at base, as designed. With the change: <strong>9 / 9</strong>. The product file was restored by sha256 after the red run.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>services/auth suite by cell name: <strong>105 files / 1200 cells, 1 failed</strong> at the base; <strong>106 files / 1209 cells, 1 failed</strong> with the change; 0 vanished, 9 new, 0 changed status. The one failure is the same cell on both sides: <code>ks949-platform-admin-seed-identity.test.ts</code> &ldquo;the enumeration actually finds seed sites&rdquo;, which ran 5005 ms against vitest&rsquo;s 5 s default under machine load 10 to 13 (a load timeout; KS 1155 names this cell).</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Type-check and lint: <code>tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json</code> rc 0. The repo&rsquo;s own test-file ratchet for services/auth examined 157 files (156 at the base), 42 errors, 42 in the baseline, 0 new. <code>eslint</code> on the two files: 0 errors and 1 warning (<code>prefer-const</code> at <code>issuerCerts.ts</code> line 738, which is line 733 at the base and lies outside this change&rsquo;s hunks).</td></tr>
+</table>
+<h3>84.2 What the cells prove, and what they do not</h3>
+<table class="pmatrix"><tr><td class="pm-topic" rowspan="2"><strong>One helper and its four callers, not the role vocabulary.</strong></td><td> R1 and R2 prove the helper exists and keeps the truth table of the lines it replaced; R3 reads the file&rsquo;s source text and proves the comparison appears once. C1 to C6 prove that the four gates admit and refuse the same callers as before: an ORG_ADMIN, lower and mixed case super_admin, an ordinary USER, a mixed-case Admin, no role, no user, and the read, write, revoke and sign scopes. This PR does not change which roles are admin roles, and it does not touch the seven divergent role lists that KS-1536 is about. </td></tr><tr><td>Not measured: the other six role lists, a running stack, the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6), a Node 24 LTS run, and any deploy. None of them is claimed as passing.
